Conceptualize it this way, maybe it will help.

You're not likely to try to kill a unicorn in
melee by attacking its horn, that's the pointy
end, and not really very likely to cause the
beast to die, you're more likely to attack its
flanks or torso, so probably dropping a horn "every
time" (does that really happen?) really makes sense.

But when you're meleeing a dragon, you're very
much attacking its scales, trying to stick something
pointy through them, and by the time you are done,
what's left might not be suitable for turning into
armor even using magic, so "scales" might drop, but
they might drop scattered all around the battle
field by your melee efforts, rather than dropping
fairly intact and suitable to wear as clumsy "dragon
scale armor" and then to further enchant into
"dragon scale mail".

Or, that rationalization might not work for you at
all!

